WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.035 --> 00:00:01.224
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:01.224 --> 00:00:04.224
Today's message is Impose Your Will.

00:00:05.309 --> 00:00:07.069
Over to you, Inky Johnson.

00:00:07.069 --> 00:00:09.019
(rooster crows)

00:00:09.019 --> 00:00:11.778
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:14.476
♫ Espresso'll keep me goin'

00:00:14.476 --> 00:00:19.325
♫ I wake up every mornin'♫

00:00:19.325 --> 00:00:20.446
- You know why people quit?

00:00:20.446 --> 00:00:23.313
People don't have pride in what they do.

00:00:23.313 --> 00:00:25.614
You know why people stop?

00:00:25.614 --> 00:00:28.234
They're selfish and it's just about them.

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:29.827
When you have a bigger
purpose to why you're doin'

00:00:29.827 --> 00:00:32.160
what you're doin', and you
want to honor the sacrifices

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.819
that others have made
for you, it's nothin'

00:00:33.819 --> 00:00:36.511
for you to keep goin'
when you hit adversity.

00:00:36.511 --> 00:00:38.681
If every decision and choice
you make is just about you,

00:00:38.681 --> 00:00:40.781
at certain point you're
going to hit somethin'

00:00:40.781 --> 00:00:42.886
that's a lot tougher than you,
and it's going to make you quit

00:00:42.886 --> 00:00:44.734
because you don't have a
drivin' force for why you do

00:00:44.734 --> 00:00:46.130
what you do.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:47.924
But when I got up to the
University of Tennessee,

00:00:47.924 --> 00:00:48.979
it was simple.

00:00:48.979 --> 00:00:51.745
It was simple for me to
give everything I had.

00:00:51.745 --> 00:00:53.264
My freshman year, I played special teams.

00:00:53.264 --> 00:00:55.064
My sophomore season I
broke the star lineup,

00:00:55.064 --> 00:00:56.781
had a really strong sophomore season.

00:00:56.781 --> 00:00:59.111
The summer headin' into my
junior year, I still remember

00:00:59.111 --> 00:01:01.039
the day while I was
sittin' in that film room,

00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:03.622
I was watchin' film on
the California Bears.

00:01:03.622 --> 00:01:06.085
My Defensive Backs Coach,
Larry Slade, came in the room

00:01:06.085 --> 00:01:08.540
he said, "Inky, I got
some good news for you."

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:10.134
I dropped the clicker,
I said, "What is it?"

00:01:10.134 --> 00:01:12.854
He said, "Man, your projected
top 30 draft pick, son."

00:01:12.854 --> 00:01:14.001
He said, "All you have to do is play

00:01:14.001 --> 00:01:15.095
"the next 10 football games.

00:01:15.095 --> 00:01:17.745
"You're an automatic multimillionaire."

00:01:17.745 --> 00:01:18.677
I went out of that room.

00:01:18.677 --> 00:01:21.355
I called my mother and my
grandmother on a three way.

00:01:21.355 --> 00:01:24.467
I said, "After this season,
there'll be no more struggle."

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:27.055
I said, "We will never miss another meal."

00:01:27.055 --> 00:01:28.759
I said, "We will never
experience another Christmas

00:01:28.759 --> 00:01:30.828
"where we have to stand
on the side of the curb

00:01:30.828 --> 00:01:32.286
"and just be grateful."

00:01:32.286 --> 00:01:33.738
Now, I hung it up.

00:01:33.738 --> 00:01:35.321
First football game, I
went out and played great.

00:01:35.321 --> 00:01:36.223
Got an interception.

00:01:36.223 --> 00:01:37.193
Shut Cal down.

00:01:37.193 --> 00:01:38.809
Second game, we kind of get scared for us.

00:01:38.809 --> 00:01:40.702
Got late in the game, fourth quarter.

00:01:40.702 --> 00:01:42.808
Guy dropped back, he threw
the ball to a receiver

00:01:42.808 --> 00:01:44.123
comin' out of my side line.

00:01:44.123 --> 00:01:45.761
Me and the guy, we went head on.

00:01:45.761 --> 00:01:47.761
Soon as I hit the guy, I
felt as if every breath

00:01:47.761 --> 00:01:49.689
in my body left.

00:01:49.689 --> 00:01:51.352
Body went completely limp.

00:01:51.352 --> 00:01:53.620
Fell to the ground and I blacked out.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:55.626
Never happened to me before.

00:01:55.626 --> 00:01:56.964
When my eyes opened, I'll never forget.

00:01:56.964 --> 00:02:00.216
My team mates ran over, they
said, "Ink, get up, let's go."

00:02:00.216 --> 00:02:01.716
I said, "I can't."

00:02:02.608 --> 00:02:05.001
I said, "I can't move."

00:02:05.001 --> 00:02:06.746
They said, "What do you
mean you can't move?

00:02:06.746 --> 00:02:08.673
"You're our lock down
quarter, man, we need you.

00:02:08.673 --> 00:02:10.232
"Let's go."

00:02:10.232 --> 00:02:12.780
I said, "I know man, but
this time I can't move."

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:15.229
I flipped my head up to
the sky and said, "God,"

00:02:15.229 --> 00:02:17.267
I said, "Surely nothin'
has happened in this moment

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:18.967
"that can alter my life."

00:02:18.967 --> 00:02:20.713
They got me over to the
hospital, they took me back,

00:02:20.713 --> 00:02:22.917
they ran CAT scans, they
brought me back into my room

00:02:22.917 --> 00:02:24.972
and all in a 15 second
time frame, the doctor came

00:02:24.972 --> 00:02:27.083
runnin' from the opposite side.

00:02:27.083 --> 00:02:28.763
He said, "Hey, get in here,
we got to rush this guy

00:02:28.763 --> 00:02:30.028
"back to emergency surgery.

00:02:30.028 --> 00:02:32.012
"He's about to die."

00:02:32.012 --> 00:02:33.262
I said, "What?"

00:02:34.122 --> 00:02:36.069
He said, "Son, you have
busted a subclavian artery

00:02:36.069 --> 00:02:36.902
"in your chest.

00:02:36.902 --> 00:02:37.735
"You're bleedin' internally.

00:02:37.735 --> 00:02:39.195
"We have to rush you
back, take the main vein

00:02:39.195 --> 00:02:40.897
"out of your left leg,
plug it into your chest

00:02:40.897 --> 00:02:43.202
"in order to save your life."

00:02:43.202 --> 00:02:44.929
When I opened my eyes from
recovery, the same doctor

00:02:44.929 --> 00:02:45.762
was over me.

00:02:45.762 --> 00:02:47.071
He said, "Son, have some good news

00:02:47.071 --> 00:02:48.021
"and some bad news for ya."

00:02:48.021 --> 00:02:49.597
I said, "You got some bad
news for me after tellin' me

00:02:49.597 --> 00:02:50.473
"I'm about to die?

00:02:50.473 --> 00:02:51.853
"I'm still alive.

00:02:51.853 --> 00:02:53.074
"How bad can it get?

00:02:53.074 --> 00:02:53.907
"I'm still here."

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:55.693
(audience giggles)

00:02:55.693 --> 00:02:57.547
He said, "The good news
is we saved your life."

00:02:57.547 --> 00:02:59.386
I said, "Thank you, sir."

00:02:59.386 --> 00:03:01.470
He said, "The bad news is,
Ink, you have nerve damage

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:02.605
"in your right shoulder."

00:03:02.605 --> 00:03:04.284
I said, "Okay, cool."

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:05.901
He said, "But son, it's
a strong possibility

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:07.647
"that you probably can never
play the game of football

00:03:07.647 --> 00:03:09.468
"again in your life."

00:03:09.468 --> 00:03:11.427
I said, "No way."

00:03:11.427 --> 00:03:14.906
I said, "No disrespect to you,
doc, but I've been workin'

00:03:14.906 --> 00:03:18.060
"for this ever since I
was seven years old."

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.358
I said, "No disrespect to you, doc,

00:03:19.358 --> 00:03:21.294
"but you wasn't in the
park with me and my mother.

00:03:21.294 --> 00:03:23.012
"And I was seven years old
and she was sittin' in that

00:03:23.012 --> 00:03:24.996
"Buick re-got when she got
done working at Wendy's.

00:03:24.996 --> 00:03:26.776
"No disrespect to you,
doc, but you didn't come up

00:03:26.776 --> 00:03:28.596
"in that two bedroom home, 14 people,

00:03:28.596 --> 00:03:29.818
"sleepin' on the floor.

00:03:29.818 --> 00:03:31.595
"No disrespect to you,
doc, but you didn't miss

00:03:31.595 --> 00:03:34.798
"those meals and stay focused
and never made an excuse."

00:03:34.798 --> 00:03:36.131
I never cheated.

00:03:37.628 --> 00:03:38.961
I never cheated.

00:03:39.922 --> 00:03:42.590
Like my conscience, still
until this day, won't let me,

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:44.479
like I can't cheat.

00:03:44.479 --> 00:03:46.739
I can't look myself in the
mirror and say, "Ink, you did

00:03:46.739 --> 00:03:48.569
"a good job" knowin' that I cheated.

00:03:48.569 --> 00:03:49.774
I can't cheat.

00:03:49.774 --> 00:03:51.903
One of the greatest pieces
of advice that my mother

00:03:51.903 --> 00:03:52.984
gave me was this.

00:03:52.984 --> 00:03:56.535
"Son, whatever you start,
you make sure you finish it."

00:03:56.535 --> 00:03:58.982
And the problem with the world
today, people get involved

00:03:58.982 --> 00:04:01.506
with things, and if they
don't like a certain person,

00:04:01.506 --> 00:04:03.440
if they don't like the
process, if it's not what they

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:06.006
thought it was, they quit.

00:04:06.006 --> 00:04:07.852
And what they don't
understand about quittin',

00:04:07.852 --> 00:04:10.968
quittin' becomes a habit
that doesn't just affect you.

00:04:10.968 --> 00:04:13.345
Later on in life, when you get
a wife and you get some kids,

00:04:13.345 --> 00:04:15.688
when you get a family, it's
going to come back to haunt you.

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:18.381
And then will one day affect them.

00:04:18.381 --> 00:04:20.429
That is why I tell you the
process is more important

00:04:20.429 --> 00:04:21.368
than the product.

00:04:21.368 --> 00:04:23.245
It's not even about the outcome for me.

00:04:23.245 --> 00:04:24.893
It's about can you take
pride in what you do

00:04:24.893 --> 00:04:26.283
as an individual?

00:04:26.283 --> 00:04:27.795
And every night, when
you look in the mirror,

00:04:27.795 --> 00:04:30.439
knowin' that you gave
everything that you had to it.

00:04:30.439 --> 00:04:31.986
And we have to get to the
point where we're willing

00:04:31.986 --> 00:04:35.331
to impose our will on certain things.

00:04:35.331 --> 00:04:37.021
Impose your will on it.

00:04:37.021 --> 00:04:40.388
My life totally changed, and
they gave me an opportunity

00:04:40.388 --> 00:04:41.221
to stop.

00:04:42.668 --> 00:04:45.326
And most people, when you give
them an opportunity to stop

00:04:45.326 --> 00:04:47.593
while they're chasin' somethin',
they take advantage of it

00:04:47.593 --> 00:04:50.087
because they feel like,
"Man, why did this have to

00:04:50.087 --> 00:04:50.920
"happen to me?"

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:52.724
I felt as if, "Why not me?"

00:04:52.724 --> 00:04:55.208
This is the perfect opportunity
to use this to be a blessing

00:04:55.208 --> 00:04:56.171
to somebody else.

00:04:56.171 --> 00:04:57.029
And you know what?

00:04:57.029 --> 00:04:58.974
It's not even about me to be truthful.

00:04:58.974 --> 00:05:00.017
It's not even about me.

00:05:00.017 --> 00:05:01.966
Now it's about repayin' the
people that invested in me

00:05:01.966 --> 00:05:04.688
and saw somethin' in me when
I couldn't see it in myself.

00:05:04.688 --> 00:05:07.372
At a certain point in life,
it just can't be about you.

00:05:07.372 --> 00:05:09.177
And the moment that we
understand that, and every day

00:05:09.177 --> 00:05:11.151
we wake up, we understand
that life is a blessin'

00:05:11.151 --> 00:05:11.984
and life is a gift.

00:05:11.984 --> 00:05:14.191
And if you were to check out
today, how would you want

00:05:14.191 --> 00:05:15.280
to be remembered?

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:16.691
It's bigger than you.

00:05:16.691 --> 00:05:19.370
- So first off, this is an
amazingly powerful clip.

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:22.244
I had never heard of Inky
before doing the research

00:05:22.244 --> 00:05:23.077
for this video.

00:05:23.077 --> 00:05:26.208
So, whoever of you guys in
Believe Nation suggested

00:05:26.208 --> 00:05:29.351
that we do him, I am grateful.

00:05:29.351 --> 00:05:30.474
Thank you so much.

00:05:30.474 --> 00:05:32.909
I'm expecting a power house of a top 10

00:05:32.909 --> 00:05:34.325
coming on Inky.

00:05:34.325 --> 00:05:36.481
My quick thoughts on this is,

00:05:36.481 --> 00:05:39.419
I'm a big believer in the Army of One.

00:05:39.419 --> 00:05:42.691
And that's where I will will
something into existence.

00:05:42.691 --> 00:05:44.201
And so, when I'm starting
off a new project

00:05:44.201 --> 00:05:47.260
that I'm passionate about, that
I want to see come to life,

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.579
that I have this idea
that maybe other people

00:05:49.579 --> 00:05:50.412
think is crazy.

00:05:50.412 --> 00:05:53.371
I'm going to will it into existence.

00:05:53.371 --> 00:05:55.219
I am going to make it happen.

00:05:55.219 --> 00:05:57.474
And at the start, I'll
involve people and say,

00:05:57.474 --> 00:05:58.394
"Hey, do you want to join me?

00:05:58.394 --> 00:05:59.227
"What do you think?

00:05:59.227 --> 00:06:00.060
"Do you want to be a part of this?"

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:01.984
Try to build up a team
and if they come on board,

00:06:01.984 --> 00:06:04.279
amazingly, we'll build
this thing together,

00:06:04.279 --> 00:06:06.387
and if they don't, if they don't like it,

00:06:06.387 --> 00:06:08.296
they don't see how they can fit,
they don't want to help out,

00:06:08.296 --> 00:06:12.724
I will be an Army of One,
and will it into existence.

00:06:12.724 --> 00:06:14.615
I will make it happen.

00:06:14.615 --> 00:06:16.708
And as we get a little more
success, then I can afford

00:06:16.708 --> 00:06:18.671
to hire somebody to come on and help me

00:06:18.671 --> 00:06:20.721
if you won't want to join me
and partner up at the beginning.

00:06:20.721 --> 00:06:22.144
That's okay.

00:06:22.144 --> 00:06:26.322
You saying no, you tellin'
me how stupid somethin' is,

00:06:26.322 --> 00:06:29.712
you tellin' me how it's not
going to work, does not impact

00:06:29.712 --> 00:06:32.158
my willingness to go and do it.

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:34.539
And I think that's where
most people fall short.

00:06:34.539 --> 00:06:38.302
You are living your life too
much from the expectations

00:06:38.302 --> 00:06:40.838
and beliefs of other people.

00:06:40.838 --> 00:06:43.029
Whether that's your family, your friends,

00:06:43.029 --> 00:06:46.607
people around you, your parents, whoever.

00:06:46.607 --> 00:06:47.440
Doctors.

00:06:48.504 --> 00:06:51.190
You're livin' your life
according to the opinions

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:53.107
and beliefs of other people.

00:06:53.107 --> 00:06:55.633
Instead of setting the
standard so high for yourself,

00:06:55.633 --> 00:06:58.070
that it doesn't matter what
the people underneath think.

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:00.532
If you set your standards for up here,

00:07:00.532 --> 00:07:02.685
and everybody else
expects you to play here,

00:07:02.685 --> 00:07:05.113
then even when you fall short,
you're harder on yourself

00:07:05.113 --> 00:07:07.861
than anybody else can be on you.

00:07:07.861 --> 00:07:10.217
You know, if I'm late for
a meeting, that might upset

00:07:10.217 --> 00:07:13.604
somebody, you know, that
person that that I'm meeting.

00:07:13.604 --> 00:07:16.464
I'm way harder on myself than
they are ever going to be,

00:07:16.464 --> 00:07:18.484
'cause I hate being late for a meeting.

00:07:18.484 --> 00:07:20.647
There's a new potential
instructor I'm looking at

00:07:20.647 --> 00:07:22.012
for my dance studio.

00:07:22.012 --> 00:07:25.631
And, she really badly wants
to become an instructor.

00:07:25.631 --> 00:07:27.582
And she's on her path and
she's learning and growing,

00:07:27.582 --> 00:07:29.525
and developing the skills
to be able to do that.

00:07:29.525 --> 00:07:31.397
And she goes home and she tells her family

00:07:31.397 --> 00:07:32.883
"Hey I want to be an instructor here.

00:07:32.883 --> 00:07:34.597
"I think I can make an impact."

00:07:34.597 --> 00:07:36.959
And her sister, the first
thing that she tells her,

00:07:36.959 --> 00:07:40.165
her sister tells her that she can't do it.

00:07:40.165 --> 00:07:41.845
Her sister tells her that
she's not good enough,

00:07:41.845 --> 00:07:43.736
that who is she that she
thinks she can be an instructor

00:07:43.736 --> 00:07:45.069
and teach dance.

00:07:46.117 --> 00:07:48.703
And for a lot of people,
that's the end, right.

00:07:48.703 --> 00:07:51.342
For a lot of people, they give up.

00:07:51.342 --> 00:07:52.414
They quit.

00:07:52.414 --> 00:07:53.609
They're done.

00:07:53.609 --> 00:07:55.899
Because your sister
thinks you can't do it,

00:07:55.899 --> 00:08:00.209
therefore you think you
can't do it and so you stop.

00:08:00.209 --> 00:08:02.294
And in life, along the path to any goal

00:08:02.294 --> 00:08:03.940
that you're trying to
accomplish, you're going to hit

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:05.441
tons of road blocks.

00:08:05.441 --> 00:08:07.169
Tons of road blocks.

00:08:07.169 --> 00:08:10.559
The challenge is the
process of overcoming those.

00:08:10.559 --> 00:08:14.396
And if you don't believe
in what you've got,

00:08:14.396 --> 00:08:18.030
you're always going to be
subject to the opinions

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.894
of other people.

00:08:19.894 --> 00:08:22.089
If you quit on your dance dream

00:08:22.089 --> 00:08:24.923
because your sister says
you're not good enough,

00:08:24.923 --> 00:08:26.200
then you're always just livin' up

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:28.652
to your sister's expectations
for what you can do.

00:08:28.652 --> 00:08:31.605
As opposed to what you want to do.

00:08:31.605 --> 00:08:33.822
And it sucks not to get
your sister's support,

00:08:33.822 --> 00:08:36.430
or your parents' support, or
your best friend's support,

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:38.536
but it doesn't matter.

00:08:38.536 --> 00:08:40.653
You don't need their support to be you.

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:41.987
You don't need their support to be

00:08:41.987 --> 00:08:43.830
the greatest version of yourself.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.774
You don't need their support to go

00:08:45.774 --> 00:08:46.772
and build your dreams.

00:08:46.772 --> 00:08:48.439
Their opinion of you

00:08:49.659 --> 00:08:51.315
does not impact

00:08:51.315 --> 00:08:53.389
your self confidence.

00:08:53.389 --> 00:08:56.972
Does not have an impact
on your self worth.

00:08:58.422 --> 00:09:01.013
If you guys love my
videos, that's amazing.

00:09:01.013 --> 00:09:03.912
If you guys hate my videos, I don't care.

00:09:03.912 --> 00:09:05.643
Can I take feedback on
how to make them better?

00:09:05.643 --> 00:09:06.847
100%.

00:09:06.847 --> 00:09:08.495
But if you don't like me, the way I talk,

00:09:08.495 --> 00:09:10.115
the way I look, the what I'm doing,

00:09:10.115 --> 00:09:12.086
doesn't matter to me.

00:09:12.086 --> 00:09:15.978
If you're constantly living your life

00:09:15.978 --> 00:09:18.502
by the opinions of other people,

00:09:18.502 --> 00:09:21.906
you're never going to go
out and live your dreams.

00:09:21.906 --> 00:09:23.678
And so it's great to involve people,

00:09:23.678 --> 00:09:25.684
it's great to get expert opinions,

00:09:25.684 --> 00:09:28.351
it's great to tell friends and family.

00:09:28.351 --> 00:09:30.117
And if they're supportive
and understanding,

00:09:30.117 --> 00:09:32.674
they can give you
resources, and knowledge,

00:09:32.674 --> 00:09:36.088
and mentorship, and advice,
and guidance, amazing.

00:09:36.088 --> 00:09:37.588
And if they can't,

00:09:38.494 --> 00:09:40.098
if they're either apathetic
and they don't care

00:09:40.098 --> 00:09:41.497
about it, or worse, they're negative

00:09:41.497 --> 00:09:42.924
and just trash your idea,

00:09:42.924 --> 00:09:44.521
doesn't matter.

00:09:44.521 --> 00:09:46.561
You're going to will it into existance.

00:09:46.561 --> 00:09:48.612
You're going to be an Army of One.

00:09:48.612 --> 00:09:50.546
Because this is your dream.

00:09:50.546 --> 00:09:52.642
And you can't blame anybody else for you

00:09:52.642 --> 00:09:54.628
not chasing your dream.

00:09:54.628 --> 00:09:55.965
If you don't go out and hit it,

00:09:55.965 --> 00:09:57.394
it's not your sister's fault.

00:09:57.394 --> 00:09:58.719
It's not your mom's fault.

00:09:58.719 --> 00:10:00.491
It's not your best friend's fault.

00:10:00.491 --> 00:10:01.824
It's your fault.

00:10:02.926 --> 00:10:04.012
So, own it.

00:10:04.012 --> 00:10:08.284
Be an Army of One and
will it into existence.

00:10:08.284 --> 00:10:09.384
So the question of the day today is

00:10:09.384 --> 00:10:12.730
I'm curious, what have you
had to will into existence?

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:14.476
Something that everybody
was told you was crazy,

00:10:14.476 --> 00:10:16.986
would never work, you have no shot,

00:10:16.986 --> 00:10:19.895
and you just made it happen.

00:10:19.895 --> 00:10:20.884
I want to hear your story.

00:10:20.884 --> 00:10:23.153
Share it, leave it down
in the comments below.

00:10:23.153 --> 00:10:25.575
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Kamiana Jardine.

00:10:25.575 --> 00:10:27.435
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:10:27.435 --> 00:10:28.555
You're One Word.

00:10:28.555 --> 00:10:31.243
I really, really, really,
really appreciate it.

00:10:31.243 --> 00:10:32.315
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:10:32.315 --> 00:10:34.414
I believe in you, I hope you continue

00:10:34.414 --> 00:10:38.537
to believe in yourself and
whatever your one word is.

00:10:38.537 --> 00:10:40.648
Much love, and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:10:40.648 --> 00:10:43.568
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:10:43.568 --> 00:10:45.902
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:10:45.902 --> 00:10:49.226
♫ Espresso'll keep me goin' ♫

